#: {{ux-lite|inline=1|fi|Mennäänkö '''meille'''?|Should we go over '''to our place'''?}}

====Usage notes====
* When the verb shows both the person and the number, the pronoun may be left out in written Finnish and is usually only used for emphasis. However, the inflected forms are often used. In colloquial Finnish, the pronoun is almost always used, even with a verb. (compare the usage of {{m-lite|fi|minä||I}}).
* See [[Appendix:Finnish dialectal variants of the personal pronouns|this appendix]] for information on the dialectal variants of {{m|fi||me}}.

====Inflection====
* Irregular (inflectional stem {{m-lite|fi||mei-}}, as if in the plural). The [[comitative]] and [[instructive]] forms don't exist; the [[abessive]] is hardly used.
* In addition to the standard set of cases, {{m-lite|fi|me}} and the other personal pronouns have a specific [[accusative]] form, {{m-lite|fi|meidät}}.
